// RULE: W19, second clause — "an `idem` key must declare a window; a window without a key
// is a static error". The first clause is checked on the relation (NL0215).
// WHY IT MATTERS: the second clause had no enforcement site. A `txn` written this way binds
// no key, so its identity is the empty string: two different transactions written the same
// way are one transaction to an idempotency store, and the window that was asked for makes
// the collision *longer*, not shorter.
// EXPECT: NL0216
// STAGE: check
fn sweep(a: Id<Account>, b: Id<Account>, m: Money<usd>) -> Result<TxnId, TxnError>
    ! { append, debit<usd>, credit<usd> }
{
    txn idem(window: 30.days) { post(debit(a, m)?, credit(b, m)) }
}
